<BaseLayout title="About — André Dreyer" description="Platform engineering and AI, from Brisbane, Australia.">
    <article>
        <h1>About</h1>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>
                Two decades between strategy and shipped software, most of it contracting, from
                Brisbane. Platform engineering and AI is where the work sits now.
            </p>
            <p>
                Three of the longer engagements went the same way: I came in for one scope and left
                having held three. Agile coach, then head of platform, then product owner. Iteration
                manager, then scrum master, then technical product manager. Solution and design
                lead, then director of product management.
            </p>
            <p>
                The work splits four ways. Agile coaching and delivery. Platform engineering and
                DevOps: pipelines as a service, infrastructure as code, observability, and more
                recently AI-assisted engineering workflows. Product management, usually standing up
                the practice, the tooling and the team from nothing. And strategy, architecture and
                portfolio work — target operating models, business reference models, lean portfolio
                management.
            </p>
            <p>
                Certifications: DASA DevOps Coach, Certified LeSS Practitioner, ICAgile Agile
                Coaching (ICP-ACC), SAFe 6 DevOps Practitioner, SAFe 6 Lean Portfolio Manager,
                Advanced Product Manager, Applied Business Architecture, and AWS Solutions Architect
                (Associate). CNCF OpenTelemetry Certified Associate is in progress.
            </p>
            <p>
                The aim in each is the same: a team and a platform that still work after the
                contract ends.
            </p>
            <p>
                This site is where the longer arguments go: what broke, what was tried first, and
                what it cost. It is not a CV and none of it is a case study. No employer or client
                is named anywhere on it, including in the posts, which is a rule in the repository
                rather than a habit. How the posts get written, and what the site is built from, is
                on the <a href="/colophon">colophon</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
        <p class="elsewhere">
            Elsewhere: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/andredreyer/" rel="me">LinkedIn</a>
        </p>
    </article>
</BaseLayout>
